 "note": [
  "Take Root API is egress-blocked from this container (curl to api.takeroot.bible returns 000). The IRV was fetched instead from the ebible mirror on raw.githubusercontent.com (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/hin_irv/usx — that collection serves USX, not USFM), all 66 books / 31,104 verses, and every span marked mined was lifted from it with a script rather than typed.",
  "Derived by measurement, not from a translator's report — and measured the opposite way round from humility-2, because this author quotes scripture constantly and prints a reference perhaps a dozen times in twenty chapters. Every quoted span of 12 characters or more was searched against the whole IRV; where it matched, the match itself named the reference. 190 of 210 distinct references matched. The remainder are spans the author DID cite and whose Hindi is ours, not the IRV's: that is the review queue. Quoted spans that neither matched nor carried a citation are not listed — they are hymn stanzas, Rowland Hill's sow, and Luther's retort to the devil, not scripture.",
  "Quotation marks MIRROR the English source, which is what the shipped Hindi books do. all-of-grace's source is a straight-quote text, so this edition is too; humility-2's is curly, and it stayed curly. Citations follow the shipped corpus: Western digits and a tight C:V colon.",
  "CITATION FORMAT — this is the one book in the job that needed its references converted rather than copied. The source cites in ROMAN numerals throughout (John iii. 16, Rom. v. 6, Ps. cxxi.), 197 spans of them. The shipped Hindi corpus uses Western digits and a tight C:V colon, so every one was converted (यूहन्ना 3:16, रोमियों 5:6, भजन संहिता 121). That conversion ADDS a digit to a block the English block did not have — the chapter number, which was a Roman numeral and so not a digit at all. Those are the 130-odd per-block digit warnings this book raises and they are all expected; the verse numbers themselves transfer unchanged.",
  "WORD BAND — this edition runs leaner than the shipped Hindi book band (1.111-1.166): 1.086, 1.109, 1.081, 1.066, 1.032, 1.113, 1.061, 1.068, 1.066, whole-book 1.079. It is consistent across all nine chapters and it is a property of the author, not a defect. The band was derived from doctrinal prose (Murray, Spurgeon); this book is anecdote and long verbatim scripture, and the IRV is compact. ch05 is the extreme (1.032) because it is very nearly all quotation. Nothing was padded to reach the band — padding is the documented failure mode.",
  "ENGLISH SOURCE DEFECTS, flagged and NOT silently repaired in the English — ch02 cites John 3:8 as \"(John 8.)\" in the middle of a discussion of John 3, dropping the chapter; the Hindi mirrors that (यूहन्ना 8) rather than quietly correcting it, so the defect stays visible for the content fix it wants. Separately, ch02's epigraph prints John 3:3 as \"cannot ENTER the kingdom of God\" — 3:3 reads \"cannot SEE\" (enter is 3:5), and the chapter's own body quotes it correctly as see, so the epigraph looks like a compositor's slip. Because it carries an explicit citation, the Hindi epigraph gives the IRV's actual 3:3 (परमेश्वर का राज्य देख नहीं सकता). A reviewer who would rather keep the author's wording should restore प्रवेश नहीं कर सकता and re-pin the verse-consistency baseline.",
  "The verse-consistency ratchet caught four Hindi verses rendered more ways than the pin allowed, and two of them were real: John 3:3 (the epigraph above) and Romans 10:17, where this edition first read परमेश्वर के वचन (following the author's \"the Word of God\") against the IRV's and he-holds-my-tomorrows's मसीह के वचन. Both were corrected to the IRV rather than pinned around. The other two — John 3:6 and John 6:68 — were the false-positive shape, where he-holds-my-tomorrows quotes one clause of the verse and this book quotes another (or the whole verse containing both). Those were briefly pinned, and then the pin was dropped: #1132 landed on main while this branch was open and taught the audit to stop counting different clauses of one verse as competing renderings, which is exactly that shape. So this edition adds NO baseline entries and loosens nothing — the merge of main removed the two it had added.",
  "Of 211 distinct references, 189 are the IRV's own wording. The remaining 22 are almost all places where the author quotes the Authorized Version's longer form of a verse the IRV renders shorter — 1 John 5:13 is the clearest case: Moody quotes the clause \"and that ye may believe on the name of the Son of God\", which the IRV simply does not have, so that clause is ours. A reviewer should decide per case whether to keep the fuller quotation the author's argument uses or to trim to the IRV and lose his emphasis."
 ]
}
